docs {
  # Service owner authorized parties scenarios

  BDD scenarios for `POST /accessmanagement/api/v1/resourceowner/authorizedparties` and its
  `serviceowner` mount.

  Each subfolder is one scenario. The files inside are the scenario steps, named
  `NN_GIVEN|WHEN|THEN|AND|CLEANUP_...` and ordered by `seq`. Scenarios are independent of
  each other and can run standalone, and anything a scenario creates it removes again, so
  the whole folder can run repeatedly against a shared environment.

  ## Request and response shape

  The subject to look up is sent in the request body as `{ "type": ..., "value": ... }`, so
  the caller and the party whose parties are requested are separate: the token identifies the
  calling service owner, the body identifies the subject. Unlike the enduser endpoint this one
  returns a bare array of parties, not a paginated envelope, so every step reads the list from
  `res.getBody()` directly.

  A party carries `partyUuid`, `name`, `organizationNumber`, `parentId`, `personId`,
  `dateOfBirth`, `partyId`, `emailId`, `type`, `unitType`, `isDeleted`,
  `onlyHierarchyElementWithNoAccess`, `authorizedAccessPackages`, `authorizedResources`,
  `authorizedRoles`, `authorizedInstances` and `subunits`. Subunits are nested under their
  main unit rather than listed at the top level.

  ## Authorization

  The endpoint is behind the resource owner policy, which accepts the
  `altinn:accessmanagement/authorizedparties.resourceowner` scope and the
  `altinn:accessmanagement/authorizedparties.admin` scope. The admin scope additionally allows
  the `orgCode` filter to name any service owner, where a plain resource owner is limited to
  its own org code. The caller is the enterprise identified by the token.

  ## Personas and fixtures

  - `test/AuthorizedParties/testdata/<env>.js`: the accounting firm tree around
    REGN_ULASTELIG_RETTFERDIG_TIGER, its clients, rightholders and deleted sole
    proprietorships. The same fixture the enduser suite uses, looked up here as a service owner.

  ## Environments

  Runs against AT22.
}
